Mike wrote:
>
> %>> How do you get LaTeX to insert continuation lines saying
> %>>
> %>>                              Question xx continued on next page
> %>
> %>Use marks and put them in the footline.
>
> The footer is already in full use:
>
> pressmark                  page                        Turn Over

``put them in the footline'' is not to take literally if we talk about
_implementation_ of some effect. It means use \@footline (or however it
is called in LaTeX) to put your bloody sentence there.
    Such a sentence should be a bit outside the ``Seitenspiegel''
(don't know the English term, perhaps `page area') anyhow.

> also, that doesn't solve the problem of the question number reappearing on
> the next page, followed by (continued)

Set a flag, utilize the headline to check for that flag.

